From f3be94e21627667b58ea1f1b52af8db01483c28b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Newton <rrnewton@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:53:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Guard SaBRe plugin finalizers in the tool domain

[hermit2, unknown-agentname, gpt-6-astra, devbig014, role=impl]

Plain Language Summary and Project Impact

Keep SaBRe plugin ELF finalizers in the tool domain. Mimalloc cleanup after guest main previously entered shared Detcore as guest clock_gettime and madvise calls. Guard only the selected plugin map while preserving its original reverse FINI_ARRAY then FINI callbacks and the caller's prior domain. Guest and dependency finalizers remain unchanged.

The retained pid-probe strict repeat pair stays matched while removing 39 allocator clocks and 7 madvise calls per execution (52 to 6 syscalls). This is focused repaired-loader evidence with the retained H839 product binary, not a current-main full-profile result; the separate startup cross-backend mismatch remains red.

Validation: selected real loader and map-control tests, cargo fmt --all -- --check, cargo clippy --offline -p reverie-sabre --tests -- -D warnings; safehermit strict SaBRe pid-probe pair, 31/31 INFO records, no relaxations.
